# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Internal agent / derived artefacts. Appended by D-035; nothing above was
# changed, and nothing here may be reverted — these are untracked BY DESIGN and
# each one is also listed in bin/check-public-surface.php's private-only set.
#
# NOTE ON WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: `.credential-guard-baseline` is NOT
# ignored. It is a tracked receipt that the credential guard READS to ratchet
# its findings, not a suppression list — ignoring it would make the guard's
# baseline disappear from a fresh clone and silently reset what it has already
# proven. It is a private-only path (so it carries `merge=ours` in
# .gitattributes), but "private" and "untracked" are different things.
#
# MECHANICAL NOTE, because it is a real trap in this file's syntax: a `#` only
# starts a comment at the BEGINNING of a line. A trailing `# text` becomes part
# of the PATTERN, so every entry below puts its comment on its own line above
# the path rather than after it. `git check-ignore` is the gate for that.

# agent working state (private, never published)
.ai/

# generated knowledge graph — derived, rebuilt by `graphify update .`
graphify-out/

# local inspection snapshots of the real app
inspection-snapshot/

# per-commit warm/ledger indexes (see also the TRACKED .warm-ledger.json)
.ledger/

# `.brain/` IS NOT IGNORED, and that is deliberate.
#
# It used to be listed here, back when it held a handful of files while the
# agent's real documentation lived under docs/ (D-035). D-036 moved that
# documentation INTO .brain/, which makes it the canonical, TRACKED home: the
# verbatim archive, the decision log, the plans, the registry and the per-lane
# transcripts all live there and must version with the repository.
#
# Gitignore is not privacy. Nothing here is kept out of the PUBLIC repository by
# being ignored — it is kept out by bin/public-manifest.txt and by the strip set
# in bin/check-public-surface.php, both of which fail the build when an internal
# path reaches the public tree. Ignoring .brain/ would only have had the effect
# of silently dropping new files from the agent's own history.

# the agent's own CI config + AGENTS.md copy, read by the opencode CI lanes
.opencode-ci/

# Firecrawl research artefacts — raw web captures, never committed
.firecrawl/

# Infection run artefacts (2026-10-17)
#
# `infection.log` and `infection-summary.json` are written by every
# `composer mutants` / `composer mutants:gate` run — they are the durable report
# that 46.33 added, and the reason a survivor list can no longer be read one run
# stale. They are OUTPUT of a run, not source: committing them would put a
# regenerable artefact in history, and the next run would show it as a spurious
# modification. The CONFIG (`infection.json5`, `infection/<area>/phpunit.xml`) is
# tracked, because that is the part a human decides.
infection.log
infection-summary.json
infection-html/

# Per-area Infection run output, same reasoning as above: a run writes
# `<area>-infection.json`, `<area>-infection.log`, `<area>-infection-summary.json`
# and `<area>-infection-per-mutator.md` next to its tracked `<area>.json5` config.
# They are regenerable; committing them makes every later run show as a spurious
# modification. The `.json5` configs stay tracked — that is the part a human decides.
infection/*-infection.json
infection/*-infection.log
infection/*-infection-summary.json
infection/*-infection-per-mutator.md

# Working scratch for the mutation slices (46.71/46.72) — per-slice timing lists,
# html reports and temp plans. Never source, never evidence.
.scratch/

# The PRIVATE composer vendor this repository's `vendor` symlink points at.
#
# WHY IT IS SEPARATE, and why the symlink exists at all: `vendor` is a TRACKED
# symlink (mode 120000), so the tree carries a pointer instead of 19,000 files.
# It pointed at `/tmp/tfdist/vendor`, which is shared by every worktree and every
# sibling repo on this host — so ONE other session's `composer install` rewrote
# the dependency tree under a running mutation gate and killed it twice with
# `Class "PhpParser\Node\Stmt\Nop" not found` and
# `Class "Symfony\Component\Process\Exception\ProcessTimedOutException" not found`
# (measured 2026-10-22 11:19:06 UTC and 11:30:54 UTC). A gate that dies because
# a stranger ran composer is not a gate.
#
# `.vendor/` is this repository's own, private copy: nothing else on this host
# writes into it, so a long gate keeps the dependency tree it started with.
# It is gitignored for the same reason `vendor/` is — it is a regenerable
# artefact, and `composer install` rebuilds it. DO NOT run `composer install`
# in this repository while a mutation gate is running: the install writes
# through the `vendor` symlink INTO `.vendor/`, which is the churn this
# directory exists to stop.
.vendor/
